{
	"Name": "AlertQuery - Okta - User - Authentication - High Number of Okta Device Tokens from One Source [table]",
	"Description": "Finds source addresses that generated an unusual number of distinct device token hashes. Each new dtHash is a new browser identity, so one address producing dozens is a tool cycling clients to get around Okta's per-device rate limiting and behaviour rules.\n\nThreshold: 10 or more distinct device token hashes from one address. Edit the eval near the end of the query to tune it.\n\nThis detection uses stats, so it renders as a table rather than shipping raw entries.\n\nReference(s):\n- https://detection.fyi/elastic/detection-rules/integrations/okta/credential_access_high_number_of_okta_device_token_cookies_generated_for_authentication/\n- https://github.com/elastic/detection-rules/tree/main/rules/integrations/okta",
	"GUID": "2ab0a09b-3585-510a-ba2f-1283fe48151b",
	"Labels": [
		"okta"
	],
	"Metadata": {
		"timeframe": null
	}
}